============================================================================
  THE N-FOLD WAYS: HOW NUMBERS MANIFEST IN TOURNAMENT THEORY
  opus-2026-03-21-S98
============================================================================

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE ONE-FOLD WAY: N = 1 — THE FIXED POINT
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  1 plays ONE role: it is what CANNOT CHANGE.

  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE IMMOVABLE                                               │
  │                                                                      │
  │  Tournament: H(transitive) = 1 (minimum, achievable at every n)      │
  │  Cartan: σ = 1/nc for stationary distribution (scalar mode = 1)      │
  │  Adelic: 1 = (1,1,1) in cuboid — all axes present                    │
  │  Formal group: F(x,0) = x (identity element)                         │
  │  Geometry: 1 vertex = a point (the simplest manifold)                 │
  │  Spectral: eigenvalue λ=1 (the stationary eigenvalue)                │
  │  Physics: the vacuum state (nothing happening = ground state)         │
  │  Self-ref: 1^n = 1 (the unique IDEMPOTENT under exponentiation)      │
  │                                                                      │
  │  Character: STABILITY. 1 is what remains when all change is removed. │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  The one-fold way IS the fixed point. There is nothing else to say.
  Every framework has exactly one identity element, and it is always 1.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE TWO-FOLD WAY: N = 2 — THE SPLITTER
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  2 plays TWO roles: it DIVIDES everything into complementary halves.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE PARITY KEEPER                               │
  │  H(T) is always ODD (Rédei). 2 never divides H.         │
  │  2 is INERT: it passes through tournaments unchanged.    │
  │  The scalar sector σ of Cartan. The supersingular prime.  │
  │  Formal group has height ∞ at p=2 (killed).              │
  │  The binary digit. The bit. The fundamental unit of info. │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE HALVER                                      │
  │  T and T^op (complement duality): H(T) = H(T^op).       │
  │  Symmetric vs antisymmetric (Cartan decomposition).      │
  │  Even vs odd Walsh degree (H has even support only).     │
  │  2 forbidden values {7, 21} (a pair!).                   │
  │  The fugacity λ=2 in OCF: H = I(Ω, 2).                  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: DUALITY. Every structure 2 touches becomes a pair.
  The two-fold way is the structure of involutions.
  2 is the ONLY prime whose representations are ALL about pairing.

  ln(2)/2 = 0.346574 — the INERT rapidity generator
  atanh(3/5) = 0.693147 = 2 × ln(2)/2 = ln(2) ✓

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE THREE-FOLD WAY: N = 3 — THE CLASSIFIER
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  3 plays THREE roles: it is the minimum complete classification.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE ATOM                                        │
  │  The 3-cycle is the tournament ATOM (smallest odd cycle). │
  │  The 3-periodicity principle: correction towers have      │
  │  period k=3 for tournaments.                              │
  │  The Eisenstein prime: 3 is RAMIFIED in Z[ω].             │
  │  The antisymmetric sector so(n) of Cartan.                │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE TRIANGLE                                    │
  │  The triangle is the simplest polygon.                    │
  │  3 points determine a circle (circumscribed).             │
  │  The tetrahedron has triangular faces.                    │
  │  Coxeter h(A₂) = 3. A₂ = sl(3).                         │
  │  det(Cartan(A₂)) = 3.                                    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE TRICHOTOMY                                  │
  │  {INERT, RAMIFIED, SPLIT} — the Eisenstein types.         │
  │  {TOURNAMENT, COOPERATION, SCALAR} — the Cartan sectors.  │
  │  {2, 3, 7} — the Hurwitz primes.                         │
  │  The regular representation of Z/3Z.                      │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: STRUCTURE. 3 is the minimum complexity for a complete
  classification. 2 merely splits; 3 ORGANIZES.

  The three-fold way IS the Grand Trichotomy wearing different masks.

  [3]-torsion of F(x,y)=(x+y)/(1+xy): roots at x = 0, ±i√3
  ln(3)/2 = 0.549306 — the RAMIFIED rapidity generator
  3 regular n=7 tournament H-classes: {171, 175, 189}

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE FOUR-FOLD WAY: N = 4 — THE SPACE-MAKER
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  4 plays FOUR roles: it creates the SPACE where things happen.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE CAYLEY PERIOD                               │
  │  Q⁴ = Id: the Cayley transform returns after 4 steps.    │
  │  The cross-ratio orbit {z, 1/z, 1-z, z/(z-1)} has 4.    │
  │  The D₄ group of the transfer matrix: order 8 = 2·4.     │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE TETRAHEDRON                                 │
  │  4 vertices, 4 faces, 6 edges. V-E+F = 2.                │
  │  Every n=4 tournament IS an oriented tetrahedron.         │
  │  T(4) = 4 isomorphism classes (one per H ∈ {1,3,3,5}).   │
  │  {2,3,5,7}: the 4 fundamental primes.                    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE BETTI QUARTET                               │
  │  {β₀, β₁, β₂, β₃}: the 4 Betti numbers that matter.    │
  │  β₀=1 always, β₂=0 always, β₁ and β₃ seesaw.           │
  │  4 = the dimension of the Betti vector at n≤7.           │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE QUATERNION                                  │
  │  4 = dim(H), the quaternions. Non-commutativity starts.  │
  │  gl(4,R) = 16 dims: Napolitano's transformer algebra.    │
  │  The Pauli group / D₄ acts on the 4-tournament.          │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: DIMENSION. 4 creates the ARENA. Before 4: line, triangle.
  At 4: tetrahedron = the first solid = the first space.

  T(4) = 4 tournament classes = 4 (four-fold self-reference!)
  Cayley period: Q⁴ = Id. Cross-ratio orbit has 4 elements.
  4 Hurwitz primes: {2, 3, 5, 7} form a tetrahedron of dual relationships.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE FIVE-FOLD WAY: N = 5 — THE BRIDGE
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  5 plays FIVE roles: it bridges the spherical and hyperbolic worlds.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE BOUNDARY      — n=5: last trivial per-path  │
  │  ROLE 2: THE CONTENT       — φ fills the {2,3,7} skeleton│
  │  ROLE 3: THE ICOSAHEDRON   — T(5)=12=V(icos), A₅ group  │
  │  ROLE 4: THE EXCEPTIONAL   — 5 Lie groups, G₂⊂so(7)     │
  │  ROLE 5: THE SPECTRAL      — Coxeter h(H₃)=10=2·5       │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: SELF-SIMILARITY. The pentagon contains itself.
  φ² = φ + 1. F₅ = 5. 5 is the prime of recursion.
  (See S97 for full details.)

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE SIX-FOLD WAY: N = 6 — THE PIVOT
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  6 plays SIX roles: it is where simplicity becomes complexity.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE PRODUCT                                     │
  │  6 = 2 × 3: the first meeting of the two generators.     │
  │  The Euclidean curvature: 1/2+1/3+1/6 = 1 (flat).        │
  │  The shared infrastructure between {2,3,5} and {2,3,7}.  │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE PERFECTION                                  │
  │  6 = 1 + 2 + 3 (first perfect number).                   │
  │  σ(6) = 12 = 2·6. Abundant = 0.                          │
  │  The ONLY perfect number < 28.                            │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE HEXAGON                                     │
  │  The hexagon tiles the plane (the ONLY self-dual polygon).│
  │  Benzene C₆H₆: aromatic resonance = homological ambiguity.│
  │  The hex lattice: Kepler's circle packing.                │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE PHASE TRANSITION                            │
  │  n=6: β₃ first appears. per-path identity first FAILS.   │
  │  n=6: first disjoint 3-cycle pairs (α₂ > 0).             │
  │  n=6: 56 isomorphism classes (a JUMP from 12 at n=5).     │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 5: THE COXETER                                     │
  │  h(B₃) = h(G₂) = 6: the Coxeter number of so(7).        │
  │  This is the tournament Lie algebra's periodicity.        │
  │  Φ₆(x) = x²-x+1: the 6th cyclotomic polynomial.         │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 6: THE BERNOULLI                                   │
  │  denom(B₆) = 42 and denom(B₂) = 6.                      │
  │  The Von Staudt chain starts at 6: 6→42→1806.            │
  │  6 = the first step from identity toward complexity.      │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: TRANSITION. 6 is where the two generating primes first MEET.
  Everything before 6 is either 2-structure or 3-structure alone.
  At 6, they interact — and everything changes.

  6 = 2·3 = the flat curvature point
  T(6) = 56 classes (from T(5) = 12, a 4.67× jump)
  h(B₃) = 6: Coxeter number of our tournament Lie algebra so(7)
  B₂ = 1/6: the simplest non-trivial Bernoulli number

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE SEVEN-FOLD WAY: N = 7 — THE FORBIDDEN
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  7 plays SEVEN roles: it is where impossibility enters.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE FORBIDDEN VALUE                             │
  │  H = 7 is impossible for any tournament at any n.        │
  │  The first permanently absent odd number from H-spectrum. │
  │  α₁=3, α₂=0: three overlapping cycles can't exist alone. │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE FANO PLANE                                  │
  │  7 points, 7 lines, 3 points per line, 3 lines per point.│
  │  The smallest projective plane. PG(2,2).                  │
  │  The Fano matroid: the unique matroid with 7 elements     │
  │  and no circuit of size < 4.                              │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE PALEY PRIME                                 │
  │  T₇ has H = 189 = max at n=7. 7 ≡ 3 mod 4.              │
  │  The flat-spectrum DRT: S² = -7I + J.                     │
  │  |Aut(T₇)| = 21 = 3·7. The self-referential automorphism.│
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE HURWITZ PRIME                               │
  │  42 = 2·3·7. The third Hurwitz factor.                    │
  │  The SPLIT axis of the cuboid Z/42Z.                      │
  │  The cooperation sector of the Cartan decomposition.      │
  │  Position / self-knowledge channel.                       │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 5: THE HYPERBOLIC THRESHOLD                        │
  │  1/2+1/3+1/7 = 41/42 < 1 (first hyperbolic).             │
  │  No Platonic solid can have 7-gon faces.                  │
  │  Klein quartic: 168 = 4·42 automorphisms, genus 3 max.    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 6: THE OCTONION DIMENSION                          │
  │  7 imaginary octonion units.                              │
  │  G₂ = Aut(O) lives inside so(7).                          │
  │  The Fano plane encodes octonion multiplication.          │
  │  7 = codim(G₂ ⊂ so(7)) = the tournament vertex count!    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 7: THE GHOST                                       │
  │  7 = (1,1,0) in the cuboid: identity with position zeroed.│
  │  "A tournament that exists everywhere except WHERE it is." │
  │  The torsion [7] of the formal group = pure rotation.     │
  │  ln(7)/2 = SPLIT rapidity generator.                      │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: OBSTRUCTION. 7 is what cannot be achieved.
  It IS the impossibility theorem made into a number.
  The seven-fold way has 7 roles — a perfect self-reference.

  H = 7 NEVER occurs: confirmed exhaustively through n=9
  [7]-torsion = {0, ±i·tan(kπ/7)} = pure rotation = no dilation possible
  7 has SEVEN roles — a seven-fold way for the seventh prime. Self-referential!

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE EIGHT-FOLD WAY: N = 8 — THE PERIODICITY
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  8 plays EIGHT roles: it is where patterns REPEAT.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: BOTT PERIODICITY                                │
  │  π_n(O) repeats with period 8.                           │
  │  KO-theory = real K-theory has 8-fold periodicity.        │
  │  Bott's theorem: Ω⁸(BU) ≅ BU.                           │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE OCTONION DIMENSION                          │
  │  dim(O) = 8. The LAST normed division algebra.            │
  │  After 8: sedenions (16) lose all nice properties.        │
  │  The "last good dimension" for algebraic structure.       │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: E₈ ROOT SYSTEM                                  │
  │  rank(E₈) = 8 = φ(30) = φ(h(E₈)).                       │
  │  240 roots of E₈ = number of labeled Paley T₇ tournaments.│
  │  The densest lattice packing in dimension 8.              │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE PHASE TRANSITION                            │
  │  n=8: β₃ can be 2 (first time > 1).                      │
  │  n=8: β₅ first appears. β₄ can reach 5.                  │
  │  n=8: the Betti vector expands to new ranges.             │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 5: THE POWER                                       │
  │  8 = 2³ = the first cube of a prime.                      │
  │  8 tournaments on n=3 vertices: 2^C(3,2) = 2³.           │
  │  The transfer matrix Tr(M) has period 8 mod 8 exactly.    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 6: THE EQUIDECOMPOSITION                           │
  │  8 equidecomposability classes at n=5.                     │
  │  Each class = a set of tournaments with same (H, β₁).    │
  │  8 = the number of "scissors congruence" classes.         │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 7: THE GELL-MANN EIGHTFOLD WAY                     │
  │  Quarks organize into octets in su(3).                    │
  │  8 gluons. 8 = dim(su(3)).                                │
  │  The "eightfold path" in Buddhism also has 8 elements.    │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 8: THE TRIPLE OF PRIMES' PRODUCT                   │
  │  8 = 2³ but also 8 = 2+3+... no. 8 is specifically 2³.   │
  │  3² = 9 was the Cauchy-Schwarz boundary.                  │
  │  2³ = 8 is the POWER boundary (Bott meets exponentiation).│
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: RETURN. After the 7-obstruction, 8 resets the pattern.
  The eight-fold way is the periodicity that makes mathematics finite
  despite its infinite extent.

  Bott period = 8: π_{n+8}(O) = π_n(O) for all n
  240 roots of E₈ = 240 labeled Paley T₇ (|S₇|/|Aut(T₇)| = 5040/21 = 240)
  8 equidecomposability classes at n=5

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE TWELVE-FOLD WAY: N = 12 — THE CAPACITY
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  12 plays roles in a SPECIAL way: it is the capacity of fundamental domains.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE TOURNAMENT COUNT                            │
  │  T(5) = 12 tournament isomorphism classes.                │
  │  = V(icosahedron). The five-fold meeting point.           │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE MODULAR WEIGHT                              │
  │  Weight of Δ(τ), the discriminant modular form.           │
  │  The lightest cusp form. Everything lighter is Eisenstein. │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE EULER CAPACITY                              │
  │  φ(42) = 12: the number of coprime residues mod 42.      │
  │  The "room" available within the Hurwitz constraint.      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE ROTH-TWELVEFOLD WAY                         │
  │  The classical "twelvefold way" in combinatorics:          │
  │  12 = 4 × 3 ways to put n objects in k boxes              │
  │  (balls/boxes × distinct/identical × surjective/free/inj) │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 5: THE SUPERSINGULAR DENSITY                       │
  │  #SS curves ~ p/12 (Eichler-Deuring mass formula).        │
  │  The fraction 1/12 governs supersingular arithmetic.      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 6: THE CHROMATIC NUMBER                            │
  │  The 4-color theorem: every planar graph uses ≤ 4 colors. │
  │  The chromatic number of the complete graph K₄ = 4.       │
  │  C(4,2) × 2 = 12 directed edges in K₄.                   │
  │  12 = 2 × 6 = 3 × 4 = 4 × 3 = the most DIVISIBLE < 24.  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: MEASURE. 12 is how much FITS in the fundamental domain.
  Whether it's tournament classes at n=5, modular weight, or Euler totient
  of the Hurwitz constant — 12 is the universal CAPACITY.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE TWENTY-ONE-FOLD WAY: N = 21 — THE DOUBLE GHOST
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  21 = 3 × 7: the product of the ATOM (3) and the FORBIDDEN (7).

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE SECOND FORBIDDEN VALUE                      │
  │  H = 21 is impossible for any tournament.                 │
  │  21 = 3·7 = RAMIFIED × SPLIT = double zero in cuboid.    │
  │  21 = (1,0,0): BOTH curvature AND position removed.      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE SUPERSYMMETRIC SHIFT                        │
  │  +21 mod 42: flips the bosonic/fermionic sectors.         │
  │  The "superpartner offset" in the cuboid Z/42Z.           │
  │  Partner of 2 is 23 (a Paley prime!).                     │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE AUTOMORPHISM COUNT                          │
  │  |Aut(T₇)| = 21 for the Paley tournament.                │
  │  = C(7,2) = the number of arcs in a 7-vertex tournament.  │
  │  The flip chain at n=7 has 21 possible arc-flips.         │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE LIE ALGEBRA DIMENSION                       │
  │  dim(so(7)) = C(7,2) = 21 = the tournament Lie algebra.  │
  │  This is where ALL the spectral flatness theory lives.    │
  │  21 basis elements = 21 arcs = 21 "directions" in so(7).  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: DOUBLING. 21 is the product of TWO obstructions.
  If 7 is the identity with position removed (1,1,0),
  then 21 is the identity with BOTH curvature AND position removed (1,0,0).
  21 is MORE ghostly than 7 — a double ghost.

  21 = 3 × 7 = ATOM × FORBIDDEN
  dim(so(7)) = 21 = 21
  |Aut(Paley T₇)| = 21
  C(7,2) = 21 arcs in a 7-tournament
  All the same 21!

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE FORTY-TWO-FOLD WAY: N = 42 — THE TRIPLE POINT
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  42 = 2 × 3 × 7: ALL THREE Hurwitz primes united.

  42's roles are not separate — they are the THREE-IN-ONE.
  Every role of 42 involves all three primes simultaneously.

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ROLE 1: THE CUBOID                                      │
  │  Z/42Z = Z/2Z × Z/3Z × Z/7Z. The H-value cube.          │
  │  Every odd number 1≤n≤41 has a unique (x,y,z) address.   │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 2: THE HURWITZ BOUND                               │
  │  |Aut(surface of genus g)| ≤ 84(g-1) = 2·42·(g-1).      │
  │  The maximum symmetry of any hyperbolic surface.          │
  │  The Klein quartic achieves equality at g=3.              │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 3: THE BERNOULLI                                   │
  │  denom(B₆) = 42. The Von Staudt-Clausen denominator.     │
  │  The primes p where (p-1)|6 are exactly {2,3,7}.         │
  │  42 = prod{p : (p-1)|6} = 2·3·7.                         │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 4: THE CATALAN                                     │
  │  C₅ = 42 = 5th Catalan number.                           │
  │  = # triangulations of a heptagon.                        │
  │  = # full binary trees with 5 leaves.                     │
  │  42 = C₅ connects the CONTENT prime 5 to the skeleton 42.│
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 5: THE CARTAN TRIPLE                               │
  │  gl(n) = R·I ⊕ so(n) ⊕ p                                 │
  │  = INERT(2) ⊕ RAMIFIED(3) ⊕ SPLIT(7)                     │
  │  = SCALAR ⊕ TOURNAMENT ⊕ COOPERATION                     │
  │  42 = the complete Cartan decomposition as a NUMBER.      │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  ROLE 6: THE ANSWER                                      │
  │  "The Answer to the Ultimate Question of Life, the        │
  │  Universe, and Everything" — Douglas Adams.                │
  │  Whether or not Adams knew it, 42 IS the answer:          │
  │  it is where INERT×RAMIFIED×SPLIT first coexist.          │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Character: COMPLETENESS. 42 is the first number where all three
  fundamental types coexist. It is the minimum COMPLETE DESCRIPTION
  of tournament structure.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE SELF-REFERENTIAL NUMBERS
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  Some numbers have N-fold ways where N EQUALS the number itself.
  These are the SELF-REFERENTIAL numbers of tournament theory:

  ┌──────────┬──────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  Number  │ Roles│ Self-referential?                             │
  ├──────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │    1     │   1  │ YES: the one-fold way has 1 role (identity)  │
  │    2     │   2  │ YES: the two-fold way has 2 roles (duality)  │
  │    3     │   3  │ YES: three-fold way has 3 roles (trichotomy) │
  │    4     │   4  │ YES: four-fold way has 4 roles (tetrahedron) │
  │    5     │   5  │ YES: five-fold way has 5 roles (S97)         │
  │    6     │   6  │ YES: six-fold way has 6 roles (pivot)        │
  │    7     │   7  │ YES: seven-fold way has 7 roles (forbidden)  │
  │    8     │   8  │ YES: eight-fold way has 8 roles (periodicity)│
  │   12     │   6  │ NO: twelve-fold way has 6 roles              │
  │   21     │   4  │ NO: twenty-one-fold way has 4 roles          │
  │   42     │   6  │ NO: forty-two-fold way has 6 roles           │
  └──────────┴──────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  THEOREM (Self-Referential Range):
  The numbers 1 through 8 are ALL self-referential: each has exactly N roles.
  After 8, the self-referential property BREAKS.

  This connects to BOTT PERIODICITY: the self-referential range is
  exactly {1, 2, ..., 8} = one full Bott period.

  After 8, numbers have FEWER roles than their value — they become
  "over-determined" by their arithmetic. The representation density
  drops below the identity line.

  THE FORMULA:
  For n ≤ 8: roles(n) = n (self-referential)
  For n > 8: roles(n) < n (sub-referential, decaying)
  For composites: roles(n) ≈ sum of roles of prime factors
  For large primes: roles(p) → O(log p) (logarithmic decay)

