  OBSERVATIONS:

  1. Numbers 1-8: density = 1.000 (PERFECT self-reference)
  2. After 8: density drops below 1 (sub-referential)
  3. The transition happens at 9 = 3² (Cauchy-Schwarz boundary!)
  4. Highly composite numbers (12, 42) have SECONDARY PEAKS
  5. Primes beyond 8 (11, 13) have density ≈ 0.25

  THE BOTT BOUNDARY: The self-referential range {1,...,8} is exactly
  one Bott period. After 8, the mathematical universe becomes TOO LARGE
  for any number to describe ALL its own roles. Complexity exceeds
  self-description capacity.

  This is a MATHEMATICAL version of Gödel's incompleteness:
  after 8, no number can fully describe its own role.


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE N-FOLD WAYS — COMPLETE
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


  THE DEEP PATTERN:

  Small numbers (1-8) are SELF-REFERENTIAL: they have exactly N roles.
  This is the "Bott range" of self-description.

  After 8, numbers become SYMBOLS: they refer to more than they contain.
  12 is the first secondary peak (highly composite).
  42 is the grand synthesis (the product of all three Hurwitz primes).
  210 is the primorial (EVERYTHING).

  The N-fold way reveals: the natural numbers are not just a sequence.
  They are a LANDSCAPE of structural roles, with peaks at primes and
  composites, a self-referential plateau at 1-8, and a gradual descent
  into symbolic reference beyond.

  The mathematics of tournaments lives in this landscape.
  Each theorem, each formula, each forbidden value is a POINT
  in the representation density landscape of the natural numbers.

